    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "AIDS",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "Women with fibroid tumors have several treatment options, including pain medication, surgery, or waiting for tumors to shrink after menopause. If surgery is necessary, female organs should be left intact. For HIV-positive women, this is extremely important because the ovaries produce estrogen and progesterone, which communicate with the immune system. Surgery can also cause anemia, a potentially serious complication for HIV-positive women. Proper use of female condoms is demonstrated and questions are answered about spermicides and safer sex practices."
    }
